WEBVTT

00:01.860 --> 00:03.150
Yuji.

00:03.520 --> 00:04.460
Hmm?

00:06.100 --> 00:08.860
You're a strong kid, so help others.

00:18.290 --> 00:21.550
Episode 41
Thunderclap, Part 2

00:21.550 --> 00:26.560
23:05      Dogenzaka, In Front of Shibuya 109

00:24.610 --> 00:27.720
In my Ten Shadows Technique,

00:28.180 --> 00:31.820
only two Demon Dogs are
granted to the user at first.

00:32.440 --> 00:37.530
The other shikigami aren't granted to the
user until they finish subjugating them.

00:38.840 --> 00:44.750
The user must continue subjugating each one
to increase the shikigami available to them,

00:44.750 --> 00:49.400
until they are finally able to
command all ten shikigami.

00:53.460 --> 00:54.620
You done?

00:55.610 --> 00:59.820
You're really strong,
just like that woman from earlier.

00:59.820 --> 01:01.130
Even though you're young.

01:01.960 --> 01:05.230
You're all beat up, yet you give
me no openings to get close.

01:05.640 --> 01:09.730
Though, with all that bleeding,
I won't even have to do anything.

01:13.650 --> 01:18.870
Thing is, this subjugation can
be done with multiple people.

01:19.080 --> 01:25.150
Though conducting the subjugation
with multiple people voids it afterward.

01:25.150 --> 01:30.990
Which means the ritual becomes
pointless to the sorcerer themselves.

01:31.900 --> 01:37.000
Still, even if it is pointless,
there are ways to use it.

01:40.640 --> 01:42.020
Who's that?

01:42.020 --> 01:43.280
They're being real flashy.

01:44.400 --> 01:46.120
To continue,

01:48.000 --> 01:52.870
while the shikigami can't be used
without first subjugating it,

01:53.530 --> 01:56.220
the user can summon them
as many times as necessary

01:56.220 --> 01:58.280
for the purpose of subjugating them.

01:58.780 --> 01:59.760
You don't mean...

02:02.630 --> 02:04.880
In all of sorcerer history, there's never been

02:04.880 --> 02:08.390
anyone who managed
to subjugate this one.

02:09.440 --> 02:13.500
Do you know why the Gojo clan
and the Zen'in clan are on bad terms?

02:14.080 --> 02:16.560
Are they actually on bad
terms in the first place?

02:16.560 --> 02:19.220
Sparks are constantly flying.

02:19.220 --> 02:22.250
Since the Edo era? Or the Keicho era?

02:22.490 --> 02:23.880
I forget when,

02:23.880 --> 02:29.140
but the heads of the clans at the time
got serious during a spectated match,

02:29.140 --> 02:30.880
and they both died.

02:31.440 --> 02:33.380
Were the heads of those clans...

02:33.970 --> 02:39.150
One was someone like me who possessed both
the Six-Eyes and the Limitless technique.

02:39.150 --> 02:43.140
And the other used the same
technique as you, Megumi.

02:44.990 --> 02:46.950
The Ten Shadows Technique.

02:49.420 --> 02:52.600
Understand what I'm getting at?

02:53.240 --> 02:57.970
That doesn't mean I can actually become
a sorcerer capable of beating you.

02:59.360 --> 03:03.740
I imagine the head of the clan used
this in much the same way back then.

03:06.060 --> 03:09.390
Sacred treasure swing and ring, ring.

03:13.120 --> 03:14.720
Sukuna-sama?

03:14.720 --> 03:16.200
Urgent business.

03:16.660 --> 03:17.990
I see.

03:18.730 --> 03:23.160
It won't be much longer before I'm free.

03:23.790 --> 03:26.540
Do not slack on our preparations.

03:26.540 --> 03:28.320
See you later, Uraume.

03:28.320 --> 03:29.400
As you wish.

03:30.400 --> 03:32.570
I'll be awaiting your return.

03:50.160 --> 03:51.360
He tricked me!

03:52.620 --> 03:53.900
He's starting that ritual!

03:53.900 --> 03:58.180
And he's forcing me to participate
in the damn thing with him!

03:58.810 --> 04:00.690
Eight-Grip Sword...

04:01.520 --> 04:03.160
Divergent Sila Divine General...

04:04.000 --> 04:05.160
Mahoraga.

04:17.520 --> 04:18.490
See you later.

04:19.030 --> 04:19.950
Yeah!

04:20.840 --> 04:22.940
Sorry, Itadori.

04:23.680 --> 04:25.970
Hey, fuckface!

04:26.460 --> 04:28.310
I'll be the one dying first.

04:28.310 --> 04:30.160
So good luck, you'll need it.

04:42.340 --> 04:43.360
Wait!

04:43.850 --> 04:46.220
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

04:46.220 --> 04:48.380
Oh, fuck you!

04:49.040 --> 04:50.380
Damn it!

04:50.600 --> 04:53.320
Wake up, you shitty sorcerer!

04:55.010 --> 04:58.060
The technique of the
curse user Shigemo Haruta

04:58.060 --> 05:03.580
erases life's little daily miracles
from his memory and stores them up.

05:03.920 --> 05:07.250
That stock manifests as the
markings under his eyes,

05:07.250 --> 05:10.850
and when he is faced with a threat
to his life, one miracle is released.

05:16.100 --> 05:20.660
However, he is unaware of this fact himself.

05:21.060 --> 05:21.890
Huh?

05:28.770 --> 05:30.560
Suspended animation, huh?

05:32.040 --> 05:33.540
I see.

05:33.720 --> 05:37.490
So saving this piece of trash
really was the right move.

05:38.140 --> 05:42.660
He probably sucked this thing into
the subjugation ritual along with him.

05:43.140 --> 05:45.970
Once this trash dies, too,
the ritual will be complete.

05:45.970 --> 05:49.080
Then Megumi Fushiguro's death
will be established, as well.

05:50.220 --> 05:51.600
Don't die on me.

05:52.000 --> 05:55.570
There are things I need you to do for me.

05:56.740 --> 05:58.760
U-Um...

05:58.760 --> 05:59.960
Silence.

06:02.550 --> 06:05.040
For Megumi Fushiguro to survive,

06:05.040 --> 06:08.210
I'll have to defeat this
shikigami as an outsider,

06:08.680 --> 06:11.980
and nullify his subjugation ritual.

06:16.280 --> 06:19.880
Time for a tasting, then.

06:25.190 --> 06:27.950
JUJUTSU KAISEN

06:53.010 --> 06:53.690
Dismantle.

07:10.200 --> 07:12.160
That sword...

07:12.160 --> 07:15.290
It's the Sword of Exorcism,
specialized in combating cursed spirits.

07:16.170 --> 07:20.080
It's packed with the same positive energy
generated by a reverse cursed technique.

07:22.050 --> 07:23.800
If I was a cursed spirit,

07:23.800 --> 07:27.120
that would have eliminated
me on the first blow.

07:29.280 --> 07:30.760
Tastes like shit.

07:41.310 --> 07:42.200
You wanna go?!

09:05.420 --> 09:07.020
Oh?

09:07.340 --> 09:09.340
You did something, didn't you?

09:48.710 --> 09:50.040
What the hell?!

10:00.550 --> 10:02.600
Now that felt odd.

10:25.900 --> 10:27.200
Again?!

10:59.780 --> 11:00.440
What is that?!

11:00.440 --> 11:01.360
Run!

11:01.360 --> 11:02.600
Help us!

11:03.050 --> 11:04.180
We're falling!

11:22.390 --> 11:23.690
Cursed energy?!

11:26.120 --> 11:28.080
You've done it now!

12:01.960 --> 12:03.910
You can see it!

12:04.320 --> 12:06.570
You see my technique!

15:46.700 --> 15:48.160
I knew it.

15:48.160 --> 15:51.110
You're similar to Yamata no Orochi.

15:51.110 --> 15:53.980
You follow my slices,

15:53.980 --> 15:56.960
and attack with cursed energy...

15:56.960 --> 16:00.110
Both started happening after
that great wheel revolved.

16:00.110 --> 16:03.050
The incantation of sacred treasures

16:03.050 --> 16:06.620
and that great wheel both represent
perfect cycles and harmony.

16:06.620 --> 16:10.630
Which suggests that this shikigami's ability

16:10.630 --> 16:13.120
is to adapt to anything and everything.

16:13.120 --> 16:15.940
It's the ultimate late-throw
rock-paper-scissors!

16:18.440 --> 16:22.810
You might have defeated me
in the state I was in back then.

16:28.400 --> 16:32.280
Now you've fascinated me, Megumi Fushiguro!

16:34.280 --> 16:36.180
Domain Expansion:

16:38.180 --> 16:40.170
Malevolent Shrine.

16:47.670 --> 16:51.350
Sukuna's Domain, Malevolent Shrine,

16:52.600 --> 16:54.360
is unlike others in that

16:54.370 --> 16:57.170
it does not cut out a
separate space with a barrier.

16:58.110 --> 17:01.720
Manifesting an innate domain
without sealing it in a barrier

17:01.720 --> 17:06.170
is like trying to paint a picture
in the air without a canvas.

17:07.060 --> 17:09.320
It's truly a divine feat.

17:10.920 --> 17:14.520
To top it off, by adding a pact to
allow its victims a path of escape,

17:14.530 --> 17:17.250
it vastly increases the range of

17:17.260 --> 17:20.630
its guaranteed-hit effect to
a maximum 200-meter radius.

17:22.630 --> 17:25.430
Though out of consideration for
its effect on Megumi Fushiguro,

17:25.440 --> 17:31.590
he has currently restrained the effect to
a 140-meter radius limited to the surface.

17:45.000 --> 17:45.840
Anything?

17:46.150 --> 17:47.570
Nope. No signal.

17:47.590 --> 17:48.540
Me too.

17:49.090 --> 17:52.090
I don't think we need to
worry that much, though.

17:53.680 --> 17:56.640
Remember the guy with the
megaphone? He should be—

17:58.360 --> 18:01.350
Sukuna's slices are comprised of two types.

18:01.840 --> 18:06.370
"Cleave" attacks things with cursed energy
in the range of his guaranteed-hit effect.

18:06.950 --> 18:09.190
"Dismantle" attacks things
without cursed energy.

18:10.290 --> 18:13.920
Both rain down endlessly upon everything
until Malevolent Shrine disappears.

18:15.990 --> 18:18.820
The only sure way to
defeat Mahoraga is to bury it

18:19.140 --> 18:23.430
with the first use of an
attack before it can adapt.

18:24.100 --> 18:26.540
Cleave would have
fulfilled those conditions,

18:26.550 --> 18:28.660
but that wouldn't necessarily hold true

18:28.670 --> 18:32.270
if it had adapted to slices in general,

18:32.840 --> 18:35.170
rather than to Dismantle.

18:54.020 --> 18:57.650
Mahoraga was close to
finishing its regeneration.

19:25.700 --> 19:26.860
Fuga.

20:19.870 --> 20:21.250
What are you looking at?

20:22.500 --> 20:23.330
Begone.

20:29.120 --> 20:32.180
E-Excuse me, then!

20:32.980 --> 20:35.300
I really am lucky!

20:35.780 --> 20:36.800
For another day...

20:36.990 --> 20:38.700
I survived!

20:41.250 --> 20:43.470
Shigemo's stock of miracles

20:43.480 --> 20:47.540
had been exhausted in his
battle with Kento Nanami.

20:50.610 --> 20:52.660
Oh, it's nearly time.

20:56.620 --> 20:57.510
Fushiguro!

20:59.390 --> 21:01.500
I just saw Itadori for a moment...

21:03.110 --> 21:05.120
No, was it Sukuna?!

21:04.070 --> 21:08.050
23:14         Dogenzaka, In Front of Shibuya 109

21:12.460 --> 21:16.150
Hey, brat, be sure to savor this.

22:01.390 --> 22:02.980
Die!

22:03.700 --> 22:05.290
Only me!

22:06.530 --> 22:08.300
Only me!

22:09.570 --> 22:10.590
Die!

22:11.880 --> 22:13.560
Right now!

23:13.200 --> 23:14.470
I have to go.

23:16.400 --> 23:17.720
I have to fight.

23:26.990 --> 23:28.940
Otherwise, I'll just be...

23:30.290 --> 23:36.330
JUJUTSU KAISEN
Shibuya Incident

23:31.130 --> 23:33.230
a murderer.

23:52.460 --> 23:54.740
This has gotten really bad!

23:54.760 --> 23:56.630
I'll count prime numbers to calm down.

23:56.640 --> 24:00.250
One, two, three... uh, nine...

24:00.260 --> 24:01.800
You missed five and seven.
